* The fast event with the pulse produced by the driver's clamp diode and switch. See tools/sim_pulse.py.
* Reference (node 0) is the controller's ground pad. Tracks: inductance with 150 ohm across (losses unknown).
.param n = 6          ; coils switched on together
.param i0 = 0.04        ; current in each coil at that moment, amperes (from the slow model)
.param tt = 1e-12        ; clamp diode charge-storage time, seconds (ASSUMED)
.param tsw = 2e-08      ; time the driver takes to switch on, seconds (ASSUMED)
.param cout = 30p       ; capacitance on each output, farads (ASSUMED)

Vbulk capp capn 8.9
LGB capn 0 130.7n
RdGB capn 0 150
L9 capp com 97.2n
Rd9 capp com 150
* the coils: a constant current for the length of the event, from the 9 V side into the outputs
Icoil com out DC {n*i0}
* the clamp diodes (n in parallel), with the forward behaviour fitted in the slow model
Dclamp out com DCL area={n}
.model DCL D(IS=7.883e-10 N=1.981 RS=1.083 TT={tt} CJO=20p)
Cout out j {n*cout}
* the driver's outputs: conductance rising from nothing to n/Ron over tsw, then the fixed drop
Vctl ctl 0 PWL(0 0 20n 0 {20n+tsw} 1)
Bsw out d1 I = V(out,d1) * (1e-9 + V(ctl) * n / 3.149)
Vdrop d1 j 0.725
LG1 j 0 92.6n
RdG1 j 0 150

LB1 j c6n 22.1n
RdB1 j c6n 150
LB2 c6n vss 7.8n
RdB2 c6n vss 150
V5 n5 0 5
L5F n5 c6p 171.0n
Rd5F n5 c6p 150
LC6 c6p c6a 1n
RC6 c6a c6b 20m
C6 c6b c6n 1u
L5B c6p vdd 90.1n
Rd5B c6p vdd 150
Cchip vdd vss 100p
Rchip vdd vss 5k
Rpu n5 hc 5k
Chc hc 0 10p
LBH hc hu 133.5n
RdBH hc hu 150
Chu hu vss 10p
Dhl vss hu DESD
Dhh hu vdd DESD
Rlo lc 0 25
LBL lc lu 133.5n
RdBL lc lu 150
Clu lu vss 10p
Dll vss lu DESD
Dlh lu vdd DESD
.model DESD D(IS=1e-12 N=1 RS=5 CJO=3p)

.control
set wr_singlescale
save all @dclamp[id]
tran 0.05n 400n
wrdata pulse_from_driver.txt v(com,j) v(vss) v(vdd,vss) v(hu,vss) v(lu,vss) i(Vbulk) @dclamp[id] v(out,j)
.endc
.end
